NNAAMMEE
       ppaappeerrccoonnff - print paper configuration information

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppaappeerrccoonnff  [ [ --pp ] _p_a_p_e_r | --dd | --aa ] [ --zz ] [ --nn | --NN ] [ --ss | --ww | --hh
       ] [ --cc | --mm | --ii ]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ppaappeerrccoonnff prints information about a given paper.  The information that
       can  be  obtained  is  the name of the paper, its size and its width or
       height.  When called without arguments, ppaappeerrccoonnff prints  the  name  of
       the  system-  or  user-specified paper, obtained by looking in order at
       the PPAAPPEERRSSIIZZEE environment variable, at the contents of the file  speci‐
       fied by the PPAAPPEERRCCOONNFF environment variable, at the contents of //eettcc//ppaa‐‐
       ppeerrssiizzee or by using lleetttteerr as a fall-back value if none  of  the  other
       alternatives are successful.  By default, width and height of the paper
       are printed in PostScript points.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --pp _p_a_p_e_r
              Specify the name of the _p_a_p_e_r about which information is asked.

       --dd     Use the default builtin paper name.

       --aa     Consider all known paper names.

       --zz     If the paper name is unknown, print it but issue  a  message  on
              the standard error and exit with a non-zero code.

       --nn     Print the name of the paper.

       --NN     Print the name of the paper with the first letter capitalized.

       --ss     Print the size (width followed by height) of the paper.

       --ww     Print the width of the paper.

       --hh     Print the height of the paper.

       --cc     Use centimetres as unit for paper size.

       --mm     Use millimetres as unit for paper size.

       --ii     Use inches as unit for paper size.


EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
       PPAAPPEERRSSIIZZEE           Paper  size to use regardless of what the papersize
                           file contains.

       PPAAPPEERRCCOONNFF           Full path to a file containing the  paper  size  to
                           use.

FFIILLEESS
       //eettcc//ppaappeerrssiizzee      Contains  the name of the system-wide default paper
                           size to be used  if  the  PPAAPPEERRSSIIZZEE  and  PPAAPPEERRCCOONNFF
                           variables are not set.

